{"title":"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Crystal has a running course marked out for her daily run. She starts this run by heading due north for one mile. She then runs northeast for one mile, then southeast for one mile. The last portion of her run takes her on a straight line back to where she started. How far, in miles is this last portion of her run?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db1e744131bc96d84b956c19ae54c5ec06affef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"397\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Crystal first runs north for one mile. Changing directions, she runs northeast for another mile. The angle difference between north and northeast is 45 degrees. She then switches directions to southeast, meaning a 90 degree angle change. The distance now from traveling north for one mile, and her current destination is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> miles, because it is the hypotenuse of a 45-45-90 triangle with side length one (mile). Therefore, Crystal's distance from her starting position, x, is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf0106f5d9eedfc2a2289180285a785376719d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{((\\sqrt{2})^2+1^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"117\" height=\"32\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f85e07c71fb200daeb9e875a79276f9b0c38b4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; draw((0,0)--(0,1)); draw((0,1)--(0,1.7071067811865476), dotted); draw((0,1)--(0.7071067811865476, 1.7071067811865476)); draw((0.7071067811865476, 1.7071067811865476)--(1.4142135623730951,1)); draw(anglemark((0.7071067811865476, 1.7071067811865476),(0,1),(0,1.7071067811865476))); label(&quot;$45^{\\circ}$&quot;, (0,1.25), NE); draw((0, 1)--(1.4142135623730951,1), dotted); draw((1.4142135623730951,1)--(0,0), green); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Crystal runs north one mile, then her next two moves can be broken up into four individual moves: for her northeast section, it forms a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangle whose legs are each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. For her southeast section, it is also a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangle whose legs are each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. Notice that the two of the legs cancel each other out; she moves north <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> units and also south <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> units. So her net movement these two moves is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> to the right. Finally, after the third move, she is at the corner of a right triangle with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. Using the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/07913c556bd7550419bd5c8d2b2aa78259c57560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d^{2}=1^{2}+\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)^{2}=1+2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"233\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d64de1ae311b57badc3bc97e0e64f43c029416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\sqrt{3} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"170\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/P7rGLXp_6es?t=132\">https://youtu.be/P7rGLXp_6es?t=132</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A\">2010 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145338\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry